      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-3),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-3)) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{(x-3)\\sqrt{1-(x-3)^{2}}})\\cdot (x-3)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-3)\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}+6x-9}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-3)\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+6x-8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
